{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Choosing a search tree"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"],"anchor":"Guides"}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a sorted set or sorted dictionary by the workload it will see."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sorted sets share one API: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SetAlgebra"},{"type":"text","text":"’s set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operations, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lowerBound(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"upperBound(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and the elements as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank. Changing which one a program uses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a change of type name:"}]},{"code":["let avl: AVLTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let redBlack: RedBlackTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let bTree: BTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let skipList: SkipList = [40, 10, 30, 20]","","Array(avl)              \/\/ [10, 20, 30, 40], and the same for the others","avl.lowerBound(25)      \/\/ 2, the index of 30","bTree.lowerBound(25)    \/\/ 2"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one takes O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") per lookup, insertion and removal (expected for the treap and skip"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list, amortized for the splay tree). They differ in the constant, in what else they offer, and in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which workloads they suit."}]},{"text":"Lookups and scans over a large set: BTree","level":3,"anchor":"Lookups-and-scans-over-a-large-set-BTree","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A B-tree node ("},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") holds tens of elements side by side, so a lookup reads a few nodes and few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cache lines, and iteration walks contiguous arrays. For a large set that is read far more often"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than it is changed, and for range scans, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"},{"type":"text","text":" is the default. Copying a B-tree shares its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nodes, and a mutated copy copies only the nodes on the path it changes. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTreeDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its sorted dictionary."}]},{"text":"Balanced binary trees: AVLTree and RedBlackTree","level":3,"anchor":"Balanced-binary-trees-AVLTree-and-RedBlackTree","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"code":"AVLTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the heights of every vertex’s subtrees within one of each other, so it is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shallowest of the binary trees and the quickest of them to search. A "},{"code":"RedBlackTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" allows a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"taller tree and in return rotates at most two or three times per insertion or removal; prefer it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when changes outnumber lookups. Both convert to a Grafluent "},{"code":"BinaryTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that shows the exact"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape. "},{"code":"AVLDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sorted dictionary in an AVL tree."}]},{"text":"Splitting and joining: Treap","level":3,"anchor":"Splitting-and-joining-Treap","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps a random priority on each vertex, which makes its shape a random binary search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree’s whatever order the elements arrive in, and gives it "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"split(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"join(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["let numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"join(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OverlappingKeys"},{"type":"text","text":" when the sets interleave. Pass a seeded generator to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap(_:using:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to make every shape reproducible. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"},{"type":"text","text":" splits too."}]},{"text":"A working set of hot elements: SplayTree","level":3,"anchor":"A-working-set-of-hot-elements-SplayTree","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"SplayTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps no balance information. ","type":"text"},{"code":"access(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and each mutation rotate the element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they reach to the root, so a run of lookups that keeps returning to a few elements finds them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"near the top:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Its other reads, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"text":" among them, leave the tree as it is, so they keep value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"semantics; use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"access(_:)"},{"text":" where the splay is wanted.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"A sorted queue with a simple structure: SkipList","level":3,"anchor":"A-sorted-queue-with-a-simple-structure-SkipList","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A skip list (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") stacks sorted linked levels, each holding about half the elements of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the one below. Its insertions touch only the levels an element reaches, and its levels are a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent graph through ","type":"text"},{"code":"layersView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Keeping every version: PersistentTreeSet","level":3,"anchor":"Keeping-every-version-PersistentTreeSet","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When old versions must stay readable, as in undo histories, snapshots handed to other tasks or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking searches, a persistent set ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees"},{"type":"text","text":") shares all but the vertices an edit touched:"}]},{"code":["let empty = PersistentTreeSet<Int>()","let one = empty.inserting(5)","let two = one.inserting(3)","let three = two.removing(5)","Array(one)                    \/\/ [5]","Array(two)                    \/\/ [3, 5]","Array(three)                  \/\/ [3]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each version costs O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":") new vertices rather than a copy of the whole tree.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeDictionary"},{"text":" is the sorted dictionary.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Summary","level":3,"anchor":"Summary","type":"heading"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Workload","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Type","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Large sets, mostly lookups, range scans"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly lookups, a binary shape to inspect"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLTree"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLDictionary"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mostly insertions and removals","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RedBlackTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Splitting and joining sets"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Repeated access to a few elements"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SplayTree","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every version kept","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PersistentTreeSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistentTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A simple sorted queue"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkipList"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/choosingasearchtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/TriesAndSuffixStructures":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/triesandsuffixstructures","title":"Tries and suffix structures","abstract":[{"text":"Search a set of keys by prefix, or a text by substring.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/persistenttrees":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTrees"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","title":"PersistentTrees","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/skiplists":{"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","title":"SkipLists","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkipLists"}]},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections","title":"GrafluentCollections","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/DecisionDiagrams":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/decisiondiagrams","title":"Decision diagrams","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Represent Boolean functions and families of sets as shared, canonical graphs."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph","role":"a